From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] isoBuilder: put installer-requestable packages on the media

The media must be able to satisfy what the installer can request at
install time. It could not: selecting "Apply STIG hardening" in the
installer asks for the STIG package set, and if those RPMs are not in the
ISO's own RPMS/ the install aborts with

  Error(1011) : No matching packages

KS_STIG_PACKAGES in stigenable.py is the installer's own declaration of
what that option installs, so import it rather than restating those names
in a package list file. Restating them is how the media and the installer
drifted apart in the first place, leaving the STIG menu offering an option
the media could not honour. The import is local because stigenable pulls
in the curses UI modules, which need not become a module-level dependency
of the ISO builder.

Packages named via --initrd-pkgs were also never added to this download
list - only the list *file* was parsed - so they could not be installed
into the initrd from the ISO's own RPMS/ either.

Both additions go to the ISO's RPMS/ only, not into self.initrd_pkgs, so
the initrd does not grow.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/photon_installer/isoBuilder.py b/photon_installer/isoBuilder.py
index 6aed7e0..ed23a5f 100755
--- a/photon_installer/isoBuilder.py
+++ b/photon_installer/isoBuilder.py
@@ -195,6 +195,22 @@ class IsoBuilder(object):
         # Add installer initrd and custom packages to package list..
         self.addPkgsToList(self.initrd_pkg_list_file)
         self.addPkgsToList(self.packageslist_file)
+        # The media must be able to satisfy what the installer can request at
+        # install time. KS_STIG_PACKAGES is the installer's own declaration of
+        # what "Apply STIG hardening" installs, so import it rather than
+        # restating those names in a package list file -- restating them is how
+        # the media and the installer drifted apart, leaving the STIG menu
+        # offering an option the media could not honour ("Error(1011) : No
+        # matching packages"). Imported locally: stigenable pulls in the curses
+        # UI modules, which need not be a module-level dependency of the ISO
+        # builder. These go to the ISO's RPMS/ only, not into self.initrd_pkgs,
+        # so the initrd does not grow.
+        from stigenable import KS_STIG_PACKAGES
+        self.pkg_list.extend(KS_STIG_PACKAGES)
+        # Packages named via --initrd-pkgs never reached this download list
+        # (only the list *file* was parsed above), so they could not be
+        # installed into the initrd from the ISO's own RPMS/ either.
+        self.pkg_list.extend(self.initrd_pkgs)
 
         linux_flavors = [
             "linux",
